{
 "esm": "1.1.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "scmstate_couple_wsm6_inputs",
  "description": "Mount-edge template library of the EqWeather-SCM state document (couplings/eqweather_scm.esm) for the eight WSM6 microphysics stages: lowers every rewrite target the stages and their nested hydrometeor_slopes (`sd`) and saturation (`sat`) subsystems read -- the column state (input_T, input_p, input_qv, input_qc, input_qr, input_qi, input_qs, input_qg, input_rho, input_ze), the start-of-call thermodynamic diagnostics (input_xl, input_cpm, input_qsat, input_rh, input_qsat_w, input_rh_w, input_qsat_i, input_rh_i) and the twenty-two inter-stage process rates the budget rescaling collects (input_praut ... input_pgevp, including the input_prevp that also opens the sequential vapour budget) -- to the matching additive coupling-target parameters, which the state document fills from its six moisture ODE states and from the upstream stage through variable_map param_to_var edges (esm-spec 9.7.10, 10.4). One library serves all eight mounts: a stage lowers only the ops it actually uses, so the unused templates are inert, and the same template reaches a stage's own parameter and its nested subsystem's parameter of the same name (EarthSciAST #313), which is what lets Melt.sd.qr_in and Sed.sd.qr_in be filled separately from Sed.qr_in. This replaces the per-stage couplings/tests/wsm6_couple_*_inputs.esm libraries of couplings/microphysics_column.esm, which lower the same ops but are split by stage because that document feeds each stage from a different dumped profile. Hand-authored; no numbers; not generated by tools/fill_tests.py and not rewritten by it.",
  "license": "MIT",
  "tags": [
   "assembly-inputs",
   "coupling",
   "eqweather-scm"
  ]
 },
